//               to collision_candidates.json or the packing conventions.
//
// WHAT THIS TESTS (the gap this closes):
//   Every prior HMAO E2E/unit test loads a world-model buffer of all zeros
//   (tb_vla_hmao_e2e.sv: `foreach (wm_mem[i]) wm_mem[i] = 32'h0;` in EVERY
//   task) or drives hmao_collision_sat directly, bypassing the AXI world-
//   model-buffer read path entirely (gen_hmao_collision_real_testbench.py).
//   This is the first test to exercise hmao_engine_top's REAL AXI read of a
//   REAL, non-trivial world model buffer, built from real nuScenes objects,
//   paired with the real W4A8-predicted ego trajectory for that same scene.
//
//   35 real (predicted-trajectory, real-object) pairs, drawn from
//   sw/hmao_payloads/collision_candidates.json (find_real_collision_candidates.py).
//   Expected-label policy (see gen_hmao_collision_e2e_dataset.py header for the
//   full rationale): clearance < -0.5 m -> assert VETO;
//   clearance > 3.0 m -> assert GRANT; otherwise BOUNDARY (log only,
//   no pass/fail assertion -- HMAO's real zonotope+SAT+ADMM decision in that
//   band is not predictable from a simple point-to-polyline distance alone).
// =============================================================================

`timescale 1ns/1ps
